// Package art fetches, ingests, and serves artwork (artwork): the
// content-addressed blob tree under <data>/art plus the art_* control
// tables it reads through *store.Store. Dependency direction api → art →
// store; art is a leaf — it never imports enrich/plugin/module. The
// enrichment chain and its pacing stay at the composition root: upstream
// URLs and kinds arrive here as plain values.
//
// # Public API (5 symbols — the ≤8 ceiling holds)
//
//   - Service: the artwork facade — Acquire (fetch-once), Ingest (the
//     per-entity crop-and-pin flow), Resolve (path-serve).
//
//   - NewService: builds Service over one *store.Store and the blob dir.
//
//   - ErrNotImage: bytes are not a decodable JPEG/PNG/WebP image (the guard
//     every fetched byte and every upload passes through).
//
//   - ErrTooLarge: bytes past the 8 MiB cap.
//
//   - KindPoster: the default art kind ("poster").
//
// # Invariants
//
//   - INV-fetch-once: one upstream fetch per (url, kind). Concurrent
//     producers collapse into a single flight (singleflight, keyed by
//     url_hash), at most 2 fetches are in flight process-wide, each is
//     bounded by a 15s budget and the 8 MiB read cap, and the hit lands in
//     art_fetches keyed by url_hash. A hash that just failed cools down
//     ~10 min in-process (the thumbRegrabber bounded-map pattern — no
//     negative rows in the value-agnostic store).
//
//   - INV-guard: every fetched byte passes the SAME guard uploads do —
//     ≤8 MiB re-check, JPEG/PNG/WebP magic sniff, then a real decode —
//     before one byte reaches disk (ErrNotImage / ErrTooLarge).
//
//   - INV-content-addressed: blobs live at <data>/art/<sha256-hex>/ and are
//     written temp+rename. The verbatim original is original.<ext>; Ingest
//     derives cropped.jpg — a center crop-once to 2:3, never upscaled,
//     always JPEG q85 — beside it, and pins the entity's art_overrides
//     selection on the art_<sha256> token. Replacing an upload deletes the
//     old pair; stale fetch rows self-heal on the next Acquire.
//
//   - INV-leaf: imports are internal/store, stdlib, golang.org/x/sync/
//     singleflight, and golang.org/x/image/webp (WebP decode-only — crops
//     are always JPEG, nothing here encodes WebP).
package art
